     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><pre dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-height:999999px;font-size:24px;line-height:28px;background-color:rgb(248,249,250);border:none;padding:10px 0.14em 10px 0px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;font-family:inherit;width:364px;white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(60,64,67)\"><span style=\"font-size:large\">Hello.</span></pre><pre dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-height:999999px;font-size:24px;line-height:28px;background-color:rgb(248,249,250);border:none;padding:10px 0.14em 10px 0px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;font-family:inherit;width:364px;white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(60,64,67)\"><span style=\"font-size:large\"> Thank you for accepting me as part of the group. Is there any way to modify the axes when I get the principal component graph? I have tried several basic R options but none have worked for me. Thanks and regards</span><br></pre><div data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\">Daryl David Cruz Flores<br>PhD Candidate<br>Centro de Investigación en Biodiversidad y Conservación (CIByC)<br>Universidad Autónoma del Estado de Morelos (UAEM), México</div></div>\r\n"
