  {
   "id": "xUchlQPgAwAJ",
   "from": "Murat Maga",
   "author": "baf6eb7bae06984d",
   "date": "2020-07-19T23:42:06Z",
   "subject": "Re:",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div>?plot.gm.prcomp gives this help page, where you can see axis1 and axis2 as the parameters you can choose to which PC you want to plot.</div><div><br></div><div><h3 style=\"color:rgb(255,255,255);background:none!important;border-color:rgb(106,106,106)!important;font-family:sans-serif;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\">Usage</h3><pre style=\"background:rgba(0,0,0,0) none repeat scroll 0% 0%;font-size:13.3333px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">## S3 method for class &#39;gm.prcomp&#39;\r\nplot(\r\n  x,\r\n  axis1 = 1,\r\n  axis2 = 2,\r\n  phylo = FALSE,\r\n  time.plot = FALSE,\r\n  phylo.par = list(tip.labels = TRUE, node.labels = TRUE, anc.states = TRUE, <a href=\"http://node.bg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://node.bg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484395599000&amp;usg=AOvVaw33YV-ISzZEdgTLgWA49Hs_\">node.bg</a> =\r\n    &quot;grey&quot;, node.cex = 1, edge.color = &quot;black&quot;, edge.width = 1, tip.txt.cex = 1,\r\n    tip.txt.col = &quot;black&quot;, tip.txt.adj = c(-0.1, -0.1), node.txt.cex = 1, node.txt.col =\r\n    &quot;grey&quot;, node.txt.adj = c(-0.1, -0.1)),\r\n  ...\r\n)\r\n</span></pre><h3 style=\"background:rgba(0,0,0,0) none repeat scroll 0% 0%!important;border-color:rgb(106,106,106)!important;font-family:sans-serif;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">Arguments</span></h3><table summary=\"R argblock\" style=\"background:rgba(0,0,0,0) none repeat scroll 0% 0%!important;font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13.3333px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><tbody><tr valign=\"top\"><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;min-width:24px;padding-right:12px;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\"><code>x</code></span></td><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:6px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">An object of class<span> </span><code style=\"background:rgba(0,0,0,0) none repeat scroll 0% 0%\"><a href=\"http://127.0.0.1:26699/help/library/geomorph/help/gm.prcomp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://127.0.0.1:26699/help/library/geomorph/help/gm.prcomp&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484395599000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2pFyIhVF9_xBK1OSSyQl2b\">gm.prcomp</a></code></span></p></td></tr><tr valign=\"top\"><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;min-width:24px;padding-right:12px;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\"><code>axis1</code></span></td><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:6px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">A value indicating which PC axis should be displayed as the X-axis (default = PC1)</span></p></td></tr><tr valign=\"top\"><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;min-width:24px;padding-right:12px;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\"><code>axis2</code></span></td><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:6px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">A value indicating which PC axis should be displayed as the Y-axis (default = PC2)</span></p></td></tr><tr valign=\"top\"><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;min-width:24px;padding-right:12px;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\"><code>phylo</code></span></td><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:6px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">A logical value indicating whether the phylogeny should be projected to PC space</span></p></td></tr><tr valign=\"top\"><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;min-width:24px;padding-right:12px;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\"><code>time.plot</code></span></td><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:6px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">A logical value indicating if a 3D plot with the phylogeny and time as the z-axis is desired</span></p></td></tr><tr valign=\"top\"><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;min-width:24px;padding-right:12px;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\"><code>phylo.par</code></span></td><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:6px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">A list of plotting parameters for the inclusion of a phylogeny, including: logicals for whether features should be included (tip.labels, nodel.labels, anc.states), toggled as TRUE/FALSE; edge parameters (edge.color, edge.width, edge.lty); node parameters (<a href=\"http://node.bg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://node.bg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484395599000&amp;usg=AOvVaw33YV-ISzZEdgTLgWA49Hs_\">node.bg</a>, node.pch, node.cex); and label parameters (tip.txt.cex, tip.txt.col, tip.txt.adj, node.txt.cex, node.txt.col, node.txt.adj).</span></p></td></tr><tr valign=\"top\"><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;min-width:24px;padding-right:12px;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\"><code>...</code></span></td><td style=\"font-family:sans-serif;font-size:10pt;border-color:rgb(102,102,102)!important\"><p style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:6px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\">other arguments passed to plot. For plots with a phylogeny, these parameters pertain to the tip values.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255)\"><br></span><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>On Sunday, July 19, 2020 at 4:23:33 PM UTC-7, Daryl David Cruz Flores wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"auto\"><pre dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-height:999999px;font-size:24px;line-height:28px;background-color:rgb(248,249,250);border:none;padding:10px 0.14em 10px 0px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;font-family:inherit;width:364px;white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(60,64,67)\"><span style=\"font-size:large\">Hello.</span></pre><pre dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-height:999999px;font-size:24px;line-height:28px;background-color:rgb(248,249,250);border:none;padding:10px 0.14em 10px 0px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;font-family:inherit;width:364px;white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(60,64,67)\"><span style=\"font-size:large\"> Thank you for accepting me as part of the group. Is there any way to modify the axes when I get the principal component graph? I have tried several basic R options but none have worked for me. Thanks and regards</span><br></pre><div>Daryl David Cruz Flores<br>PhD Candidate<br>Centro de Investigación en Biodiversidad y Conservación (CIByC)<br>Universidad Autónoma del Estado de Morelos (UAEM), México</div></div>\r\n</blockquote></div>"
